report the battery by its source instead of denying it

`report()` printed "battery no battery" on a device whose battery indicator
works. The field reports `self.battery`, the `/sys/class/power_supply`
directory, which this device does not have at all -- while `battery()` checks
`/customer/app/axp_test` first and succeeds, which is what 0004 added and what
Allium reads too.

Not a cosmetic complaint: the line was taken at face value and a solved problem
was reported as an open gap, days after the indicator started working, against
a notes/hardware.md section that said otherwise. The third such instrument this
week, after a missing "emu: save ram" line on a cart that saves fine and the
ring's "0 starved" while the codec ran dry every window.

So name the source: the sysfs directory's leaf when there is one, the vendor
tool's when that is what will be read, and "no battery" only when neither
exists. The check is `is_file`, the same test `axp_battery` opens with, so
describing the platform still costs no exec.

The test goes in the middle of the file rather than the end, deliberately:
0008 appends its tests at EOF, and anything after them stops that patch
reverse-applying, which is how `task patch` decides a patch is already applied.

Applies on top of 0004, which added the fallback, and 0008, which owns the
backlight arm just above the line this changes.

diff --git a/crates/slot-power/src/device.rs b/crates/slot-power/src/device.rs
index a63373a..0636e62 100644
--- a/crates/slot-power/src/device.rs
+++ b/crates/slot-power/src/device.rs
@@ -245,11 +245,21 @@ impl DevicePlatform {
             Some(m) => format!("motor {}", m.name),
             None => "no motor".to_string(),
         };
+        // Named by its source rather than called absent. There is no
+        // /sys/class/power_supply on this device at all, so this field read
+        // "no battery" while the indicator worked perfectly off the vendor
+        // tool -- and it was taken at face value and reported as an open
+        // problem days after the fact. A field that describes one of two
+        // sources should not go quiet about the other.
+        let battery = match &self.battery {
+            Some(dir) => leaf(dir),
+            None if Path::new(AXP_TOOL).is_file() => leaf(Path::new(AXP_TOOL)),
+            None => "no battery".to_string(),
+        };
         format!(
-            "backlight {} (0 to {}), battery {}, {}, {motor}",
+            "backlight {} (0 to {}), battery {battery}, {}, {motor}",
             backlight,
             self.max_brightness,
-            name(&self.battery, "no battery"),
             name(&self.rtc, "no rtc"),
         )
     }
